From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: encoder colour contexts (ICC in PNG/JPEG/TIFF), JPEG ICC decode, thumbnail/preview/metadata state errors

IWICBitmapFrameEncode::SetColorContexts was E_NOTIMPL on every encoder. On
the PNG, JPEG and TIFF encoders it now keeps the first profile of the list
(an empty list clears it, a new list replaces the old one, Exif colour space
contexts have no bytes to embed) and writes it: an iCCP chunk for PNG (a profile
libpng rejects is left out with a warning instead of failing the image), APP2
"ICC_PROFILE" segments of up to 65519 bytes for JPEG, the ICCProfile tag for TIFF.
The JPEG decoder now reads those segments back (joined by sequence number,
refusing duplicates, gaps and disagreeing counts) and reports a colour context
instead of the unsupported flag.

The BMP, GIF and DDS encoders validate the list and answer
WINCODEC_ERR_UNSUPPORTEDOPERATION. Frame and encoder SetColorContexts,
SetThumbnail, SetPreview and the encoder GetMetadataQueryWriter check their
arguments (E_INVALIDARG), the initialised state (WINCODEC_ERR_NOTINITIALIZED) and
for frames the written state (WINCODEC_ERR_WRONGSTATE) and then answer
WINCODEC_ERR_UNSUPPORTEDOPERATION, replacing E_NOTIMPL and FIXME noise.
